WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
(Transcribed by UniScribe (https://www.uniscribe.co). Upgrade to remove this message.)

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:07.830
- You know, 10 years ago, there would be that one person that walks into the bar,

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:13.750
looks at the bartender, says,"An old fashioned."And I always felt terrible to

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.510
charge them for this drink. I love old fashions.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.270
They have their place in my heart for sure.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:22.909
There used to be a time when another recipe of the old fashioned was more prevalent

00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:25.649
and more common. It's made actually with muddled fruits.

00:00:25.709 --> 00:00:31.449
But this one is the older recipe, two kinds of sugar.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.989
They are really important in our opinion because the unprocessed flavor of the brown

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:39.829
sugar really enhances the flavor profile and the depth on the palate.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.610
Bitters, we use two kinds, orange bitters and angosturas.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.469
and a splash of water. Then we add two ounces of George Dickel whiskey.

00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:54.030
You need to break down all that sugar and make sure that it all releases into the

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.009
cocktail. So make sure that you stir up the cocktail before you add ice.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.349
We chill it by stirring it and then we pour it over.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.969
A few cubes of ice will suffice.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.709
I choose to put two kinds of garnishes in there, a lemon twist and an orange twist,

00:01:10.709 --> 00:01:14.549
just to finish it off and bring the cocktail to life.

